 "_purpose": "What `key_tile.py --selftest` checks the closed form against: the measured `family_cells.key_tiles` and `family_cells.interaction_by_family.key_tiles.cells` of every recorded 8B layer segment, so the check runs with no artifacts directory and no path into another repository.",
 "_source": "Copied from the zk-results run outputs each point names: `runs/<run>/<output>`, `result.chunks[].family_cells` for a decode run and `result.point.family_cells` for a digest run. Nothing is derived and nothing is rounded. The two decode runs prove 32 layer segments per token block and every one of them carries the same two numbers; `segments` says how many agreed, and `segment` names the first.",
 "_shape": "`shape` is what every point shares; a point repeats only what differs from it. The fields are the prover's own `params`, and `rope` is `params.rope != null`, which is what turns the root-equality claims on.",
